    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Logic** \u2014 in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the code is assigned right before saving a new owner:\n```java\nprivate String buildCustomerCode(String lastName) {\n    String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\n    int sequence = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1;\n    return String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence);\n}\n```\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`.\n- `NNNN` = one more than the current owner count, zero-padded to 4 digits (e.g. `SMI-0007`). Computed before the save, so consecutively created owners get consecutive numbers (the test's `cb == ca + 1`).\n\n**Plumbing to persist and expose it:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, plus getter/setter.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 extended the seed `INSERT`s with a `NULL` for the new column (the tested DB uses value-list inserts; h2/postgres use explicit column lists and needed no change; mysql uses `INSERT IGNORE` per existing convention).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
